@startuml
title SIC/XE — Instruction and Operand Relationship
top to bottom direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam nodesep 18
skinparam ranksep 24
hide empty members

class DecodedInstruction {
  - m_implementation : const IInstruction*
  - m_operand : optional<Operands>
  + execute() : uint8_t
  - resolve_operand(...) : Operands
}

class "Operands\nstd::variant<...>" as Operands {
  ValueOperand
  AddressOperand
  FloatOperand
  NoneOperand
  RegisterOperand
  RegistersOperand
  RegisterValueOperand
}

class Operand <<base>>

class ValueOperand {
  + value : Word
}
class AddressOperand {
  + address : Word
}
class FloatOperand {
  + value : Float
}
class NoneOperand
class RegisterOperand {
  + r1 : RegisterID
}
class RegistersOperand {
  + r1 : RegisterID
  + r2 : RegisterID
}
class RegisterValueOperand {
  + r1 : RegisterID
  + v2 : Word
}

Operand <|-- ValueOperand
Operand <|-- AddressOperand
Operand <|-- FloatOperand
Operand <|-- NoneOperand
Operand <|-- RegisterOperand
Operand <|-- RegistersOperand
Operand <|-- RegisterValueOperand

DecodedInstruction *-- Operands : stores resolved operand
Operands ..> ValueOperand
Operands ..> AddressOperand
Operands ..> FloatOperand
Operands ..> NoneOperand
Operands ..> RegisterOperand
Operands ..> RegistersOperand
Operands ..> RegisterValueOperand

class IInstruction <<polymorphic base>> {
  + execute(context, ValueOperand) : bool
  + execute(context, AddressOperand) : bool
  + execute(context, FloatOperand) : bool
  + execute(context, NoneOperand) : bool
  + execute(context, RegisterOperand) : bool
  + execute(context, RegistersOperand) : bool
  + execute(context, RegisterValueOperand) : bool
}

class "Concrete instructions" as ConcreteInstructions

IInstruction <|-- ConcreteInstructions
DecodedInstruction --> IInstruction : invokes m_implementation

class InstructionSet {
  + findByOpcode(opcode) : InstructionData*
}
class InstructionData {
  + description : InstructionDescription
  + implementation : IInstruction*
}
class InstructionDescription {
  + mnemonic : string
  + operand_type : OperandType
}

InstructionSet --> InstructionData : opcode lookup
InstructionData --> InstructionDescription
InstructionData --> IInstruction : selected implementation
DecodedInstruction ..> InstructionSet : resolves opcode and operand type

class ExecutionContext
IInstruction ..> ExecutionContext : receives during execute()

class "Example concrete instructions" as Examples {
  AddInstruction
  JgtInstruction
  AddFInstruction
  ClearInstruction
  CompRInstruction
  ShiftLInstruction
  RsubInstruction
}

Examples ..> ValueOperand : AddInstruction
Examples ..> AddressOperand : JgtInstruction
Examples ..> FloatOperand : AddFInstruction
Examples ..> RegisterOperand : ClearInstruction
Examples ..> RegistersOperand : CompRInstruction
Examples ..> RegisterValueOperand : ShiftLInstruction
Examples ..> NoneOperand : RsubInstruction

note right of DecodedInstruction
  Construction resolves the operand into one
  of the variant's concrete types.

  execute() visits that variant and calls
  m_implementation->execute(context, operand).
end note

note right of IInstruction
  These are overloaded virtual methods.
  Their base implementations throw
  UnimplementedInstruction.

  Each concrete instruction overrides
  the overload for its operand type.
end note

@enduml